<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n57423" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κί̆ναδ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εος</span>,
			τό, Sicil. word for <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fox</i> (Sch. <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				5.25
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				514.13
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Call.Com.
				1
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>: hence, <i>cunning rogue</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὐπίτριπτον κίναδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					103
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ συκοφάντα καὶ ἐπίτριπτον κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					And.
					1.99
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυκνότατον κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					430
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Nu.</u>
				448
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.162
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				242
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
			</span></i> l.c. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ κίναδε, ὦ
			κιναδεῦ</span> codd.): generally, <i>beast, monster</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Democr.
				259
			</span></i>.</div>
